 "asked_at": "2026-10-17T05:05+08:00",
 "answer": "Singapore is currently experiencing an active haze episode, with air quality reaching **unhealthy to very unhealthy** levels in various parts of the island due to smoke haze drifting from regional fires. \n\n* **24-hour PSI:** Generally ranges across regions from the **Unhealthy to Very Unhealthy** bands (with recent readings spanning roughly **148 to over 220** depending on the region). \n* **1-hour PM2.5:** Continues to fluctuate in elevated bands, reflecting immediate changes in smoke density.\n\n**Health Advisories & Recommendations:**\n* **General Public:** Avoid prolonged or heavy outdoor exertion. Reduce vigorous outdoor activities, especially if you experience eye irritation, coughing, or a sore throat.\n* **Elderly, Pregnant Women, Children, and Those with Chronic Conditions:** Avoid outdoor physical exertion entirely. Keep medication on hand and consult a doctor if you feel unwell. \n\nBecause air quality can shift rapidly depending on wind directions and weather patterns, it is best to check the real-time updates directly via the **National Environment Agency (NEA)** or the **myENV app** before heading outdoors.",
